---
import PlatformLayout from "../../../layouts/PlatformLayout.astro";
export const prerender = true;
---
<PlatformLayout
    title="Kéire Hub for Windows"
    description="Get the latest catalog-verified Kéire Hub installer for supported Windows systems."
    active="downloads"
>
    <section class="platform-section">
        <div class="platform-shell product-details">
            <article class="prose">
                <p class="eyebrow">Windows 10 + 11 · x86-64</p>
                <h1>Install Kéire through Hub.</h1>
                <p class="lead">
                    Kéire Hub and Editor 0.4.8 hot patch are active in signed catalog sequence 27.
                    Hub downloads appear only from an unexpired signed catalog record,
                    and its artifact SHA-256 remains visible before installation.
                </p>
                <div class="download-card notice-panel" data-platform="windows">
                    <p data-download-state>Checking the active signed catalog for Windows…</p>
                    <div class="download-variants" data-download-variants></div>
                </div>
                <p>
                    The Ed25519-signed Kéire catalog verifies release metadata and the complete installer hash.
                    The current EXE is not Authenticode-signed, so Windows may display an unknown-publisher warning.
                    Verify the displayed SHA-256 before running it.
                </p>
                <aside class="notice-panel">
                    <strong>Installing the 0.4.8 hot patch</strong>
                    <p>
                        This hot patch keeps version 0.4.8 and fixes custom Editor install folders, Hub setup
                        maintenance choices, and browser sign-in messages.
                        Download and run the latest Hub installer, even if 0.4.8 is already installed.
                        Setup offers repair, uninstall, or installation in a new location.
                        Close any running Editor before installing Editor 0.4.8 through Hub or the installer below.
                        Older in-app updaters require an Authenticode signature and cannot launch the unsigned installer.
                    </p>
                </aside>
                <h2>Manual Editor installer</h2>
                <p>
                    Direct Editor installation for Windows. Unsigned Windows installer;
                    use Hub for signed package verification.
                </p>
                <p>
                    <a class="text-action" href="/preview-downloads/keire-editor-windows-x86_64-0.4.8-77faa0de86caccfb-setup.exe">
                        Download Editor 0.4.8 for Windows x86-64
                    </a>
                    &middot;
                    <a href="/preview-downloads/keire-editor-windows-x86_64-0.4.8-77faa0de86caccfb-setup.exe.sha256">SHA-256 checksum file</a>
                </p>
                <p>SHA-256: <code>77faa0de86caccfbe617fff83b386cc453e599e913cc3a09d33650169e8035ab</code></p>
                <h2>What Hub installs</h2>
                <p>
                    Hub remains separate from Editors and projects. It manages versioned Editor installations,
                    compatible Build Support, templates, package tasks, and project launch.
                </p>
            </article>
            <aside>
                <dl class="fact-list">
                    <div>
                        <dt>Release target</dt>
                        <dd>0.4.8</dd>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                        <dt>Active package</dt>
                        <dd>0.4.8</dd>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                        <dt>Architecture</dt>
                        <dd>x86-64</dd>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                        <dt>OS</dt>
                        <dd>Windows 10 or 11</dd>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                        <dt>Availability</dt>
                        <dd>Signed catalog controlled</dd>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                        <dt>Integrity</dt>
                        <dd>Signed catalog + SHA-256 required</dd>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                        <dt>Native signing</dt>
                        <dd>Not Authenticode-signed</dd>
                    </div>
                </dl>
            </aside>
        </div>
    </section>
</PlatformLayout>
<script src="/assets/downloads.js" defer></script>
